{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Cursed are you above all.</b> That he attains his desires and needs with distress and deprivation of pleasure more than all other living creatures, as they said: \"If you see a beast or bird that are skilled craftsmen, they earn their livelihood without distress\" (Kiddushin 82b). And this is explained by His saying <b>upon your belly you shall go</b> — that you shall attain your food with distress, as they said (Berakhot 58a): \"I have made my deeds worse and have diminished my livelihood,\" and they said: how many labors the first man labored before he ate a piece of bread." "<b>And dust you shall eat.</b> That you shall not attain the pleasure you had before the sin in food, drink, and marital relations, as happened to Israel in their sin, as they said (Sotah 49b): \"Purity removed the taste and the smell, and the tithes removed the fatness of the grain.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The rabbinic quotation from Kiddushin concerns creatures whose traits resemble skilled trade-craft; I render בני אומנות literally as 'skilled craftsmen' per the Talmudic idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:53.795015480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}